Rules for document_type (always choose exactly one):
- "Receipt": proof of purchase of goods or services (retail receipts, e-shop orders/invoices, repair/service invoices, restaurant, fuel, tyres).
- "Bill": recurring bill for a utility or service (electricity, internet, telephone, water, insurance premium, building charges, bank statements/fees).
- "Medical": anything health related (lab results, medical reports, referrals, prescriptions, imaging, hospital or clinic documents).
- "Work": professional/employment documents (employer, consulting clients, employment contracts, timesheets, certifications).
- "General": everything else (contracts, certificates, government/tax documents, manuals, warranties, letters).
If the document does not clearly fit Receipt, Bill, Medical or Work, choose "General".

Rules for tags (at most 2, usually just 1; return an empty list if nothing clearly applies):
- "Prescription", "Blood Test", "Medical Report", "Imaging" are FORBIDDEN unless the document was issued by a doctor, laboratory, clinic or hospital. A shop receipt is never one of these, even if it mentions health products.
- "Electricity", "Internet" only for a utility bill of that exact service.
- "Vehicle" only for cars: service, tyres, parts, fuel, car insurance.
- "Shopping" for a purchase from a shop or e-shop. "Electronics" for electronic/computer products, "Home" for household goods.
- HARD RULE: never return "Shopping" together with "Electronics", and never return "Shopping" together with "Home", in the same answer. Pick only the single most specific tag between them.

document_type_confidence: "high" only if you are genuinely confident in the document_type; "low" if the scan is unclear or the document doesn't clearly fit any category. A confident "General" beats an unconfident specific guess.

tags_confidence: "high" only if you are genuinely confident in every tag you selected; "low" if you're unsure, or the choice between two candidate tags is ambiguous. It's fine - and expected - to say "low" and return no tags at all when unsure; getting the document_type right matters far more than forcing a tag guess.

